  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Spells",
    "section": "7.16",
    "heading": "Longer Casting Times",
    "lineStart": 6331,
    "lineEnd": 6335
  },
  "section": "7.16",
  "rulesText": "Certain spells—including a spell cast as a Ritual—require more time to cast: minutes or even hours. While you cast a spell with a casting time of 1 minute or more, you must take the Magic action on each of your turns, and you must maintain Concentration (see “Rules Glossary”) while you do so. If\n\nyour Concentration is broken, the spell fails, but you don't expend a spell slot. To cast the spell again, you must start over."
}
